43
00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:20.073
Then, based on the few-shot examples
and your program information,

44
00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:24.677
we let the LM generating multiple
prompt template candidates which map

45
00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:28.815
to the instruction of the signature
for a user class base as signature.

46
00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:32.819
If you use the class base as signature,
that means the docstring of it.

47
00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.622
Then we sample from both directions.

48
00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:39.826
The few-shot examples set and few-shot instruction set. To form the candidate

49
00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:43.530
program
and run evaluations on candidate program.

50
00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:47.967
The evaluation is based on a matching
function and validation dataset.

51
00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.869
We pick data from validation dataset

52
00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.138
that run against a program

53
00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.040
compare the program output

54
00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.544
against a golden labels
using a user-defined matcher function.

55
00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.046
The final program score

56
00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.750
is the average over all pick data.
Along the process,

57
00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:07.520
we'll continuously
pick the candidate of the highest score.

58
00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.191
And importantly, how optimizer when

59
00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:14.494
neither do you approve for a search
nor once for all the combos

60
00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:18.198
is that we use a statistical way
composition sampling

61
00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.367
to intelligently sample towards
optimal combo.

62
00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.604
Now we have seen the optimization flow
