65
00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:32.545
Few-shot examples are generated
through the process called bootstrapping.

66
00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.080
This is very simple.

67
00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.018
We grab data from a training dataset
and fit into a DSPy program,

68
00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:42.322
which can be one module
or multiple modules.

69
00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:45.258
Then if according to the matching
function does

70
00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:49.762
a score over a threshold set by the user,
we crop the trace

71
00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:53.132
which is the input
and output of each module.

72
00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.402
To make that as a few-shot example
candidate for that module.

73
00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.540
Please note
that one data can generate multiple traces

74
00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:05.311
because we add randomness to each call via
certain temperature to non-zero.

75
00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:08.615
Now let's talk about how we build
an instruction candidates.

